' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Notes. The facts a reader of the skeleton cannot recover.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

note top of job_definition_handler
  Generated from the entity model, with the repository,
  mapper, entity, service and history provider beside
  it. The handler proves the request, checks
  scheduler::job_definitions:write or :delete, and
  reports what the service decided through the response
  result.
end note

note top of job_definition_repository
  Generated. read_latest_by_job_name comes from the
  model's natural key, and read_all_active is the one
  paste block: the scheduler loop fires system jobs as
  well as tenant ones, so it cannot read through the
  tenant-scoped set.
end note

note top of job_instance_repository
  Hand-written. The component's one entity with no model
  yet, so its repository, mapper and entity stay
  hand-written until that unit lands.
end note

note top of registrar
  The component's composition point. It is hand-written
  because it composes three generated families -- the
  entity sub-registrar, the history provider and the
  service-side event mapping -- with two hand-written
  view handlers.
end note

note top of action_handler
  One interface, three implementations. The loop holds
  them as unique_ptr and picks the one whose action_type
  the job states, so adding an action type adds an
  implementation and no branch.
end note

note top of scheduler_loop
  Reads every active job across every tenant, fires each
  due one, records a job instance per execution and
  publishes scheduler.v1.job-instance-events. Nothing in
  the tree subscribes to that subject today.
end note


